{
  "name": "OpsPilot - Lead Intelligence",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lead-intelligence",
        "authentication": "headerAuth",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "c713b953-64bb-4ba5-8c86-2166639aa308",
      "name": "01 Receive Lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [240, 300],
      "webhookId": "opspilot-lead-intelligence",
      "notes": "Triggered by services/n8n/triggerWorkflow.ts after a lead is created. Authenticated via a Header Auth credential (see docs/lead-intelligence.md) — set this up manually after import, it is never stored in this JSON.",
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "opspilot-webhook-secret",
          "name": "OpsPilot Webhook Secret"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "has-lead-id",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.leadId }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "notEmpty", "singleValue": true }
            },
            {
              "id": "has-execution-id",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.executionId }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "notEmpty", "singleValue": true }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "96047469-a008-48a1-b0cd-27c90cd97481",
      "name": "02 Validate Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [460, 300],
      "notes": "Payload-shape validation only (leadId/executionId present) — the lead itself was already validated with Zod when it was created. This just guards against a malformed or malicious webhook call."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.APP_BASE_URL + '/api/leads/' + $json.body.leadId + '/analyze' }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            { "name": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
            { "name": "X-Webhook-Secret", "value": "={{ $env.N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET }}" }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ executionId: $json.body.executionId }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 35000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true,
              "responseFormat": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "6c8f972e-368a-43ef-b126-e17ae4a55ece",
      "name": "03 Analyze Lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [680, 220],
      "notes": "The entire business-logic pipeline runs server-side inside this one call — duplicate/idempotency check, Claude call, Zod validation of the AI output, business rules, persisting lead_scores, creating an approval if required, updating the execution record, and writing audit log entries. See services/leads/analyzeLeadPipeline.ts. n8n does not reimplement any of this; it only orchestrates around it. 'neverError' is on so this node's output (success or failure) can be forwarded to the caller instead of halting the workflow."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": "={{ $json.success ? 200 : 422 }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "ca3029f5-356e-4ce0-af31-0e2e6d526505",
      "name": "04 Respond With Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [900, 220],
      "notes": "Forwards the analyze endpoint's own response (success/failure, leadScoreId, requiresApproval, recommendedAction, or error) straight back to the caller — the createLeadAndAnalyze() server action awaits this to show the result in the UI immediately."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { success: false, error: 'leadId and executionId are required' } }}",
        "options": { "responseCode": 400 }
      },
      "id": "79424ddb-c609-4b89-8ac9-cef717b6a25d",
      "name": "05 Respond Invalid Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [680, 420]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "01 Receive Lead": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "02 Validate Input", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
    },
    "02 Validate Input": {
      "main": [
        [{ "node": "03 Analyze Lead", "type": "main", "index": 0 }],
        [{ "node": "05 Respond Invalid Request", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]
      ]
    },
    "03 Analyze Lead": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "04 Respond With Result", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
    }
  },
  "active": false,
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "id": "opspilot-lead-intelligence",
  "tags": []
}
